# Hat in Hand (windurst 0) at GIL_RATE 1.125 (exact in binary; setting <NAME> <decimal>, quest rework P5): tier 1's 300
# gil is 337.5, a product that ends in exactly one half, so the rounding shows: npcUtil.completeQuest passes 300 x 1.125
# to addGil and to GIL_OBTAINED's parameter, which the engine reads with sol's integral getter (llround: 338; a
# truncation would give 337, reading the rate as a whole number first 300). Accepted with the New Model Hat (GMs), count
# 0: 52 (tier 1), option 1: 338 gil, GIL_OBTAINED 338, fame 10, the vars 0, completed, the hat taken, needToZone.
char zone=WindurstWaters pos=-65.0,-2.9,-145.7 job=WAR lvl=75
setting GIL_RATE 1.125
quest Windurst.HatInHand accepted
keyitem NewModelHat
login
trigger Baren-Moren                     # the hat, count 0: 52 (tier 1)
finish option=1                         # 338 gil; GIL_OBTAINED 338; completed; the hat taken; needToZone
